summary:
Ichino and Prasanna construct Hodge classes that realize the Jacquet–Langlands correspondence between quaternionic Shimura varieties. For quaternion algebras B_1, B_2 over a totally real field F, split at the same infinite places Σ and both ramified at some infinite place, and a Hilbert newform π of even weight and trivial central character transferring to both, the π-isotypic parts V_{B_1,π_1} and V_{B_2,π_2} of the middle cohomology are isomorphic as L-Hodge structures through a Hodge class on the product (Theorems 1, 3.2, 12.4). Assuming Kottwitz's conjecture for unitary similitude Shimura varieties, the class is also Tate, so the ℓ-adic maps are Galois-equivariant.

The proof:
- passes from B_1^× × B_2^× to U(2,2)-type groups GU_E(B_1 ⊕ B_2) through an exceptional isomorphism PGU_E(𝕍) ≅ PGU_B(Ṽ)^0 with a quaternionic orthogonal group of type O(4,2);
- builds a class there as the theta lift of a Kudla–Millson/Funke–Millson Schwartz form, and restricts it through a seesaw to triple product integrals for GL_2 to prove that its restriction to Sh_{B_1} × Sh_{B_2} is non-zero;
- shows via the U(2,2) Adams–Johnson packet (or a direct theta argument) and Zucker's Hodge-type computation that the relevant Hecke eigenspace is purely of type (d, d), and that Kottwitz's conjecture forces trivial Galois action;
- descends the coefficients with a determinant argument.
It rests on new splittings of the metaplectic cover over quaternionic similitude dual pairs (Appendix A).

The atlas plans Shimura data and canonical models, pure Hodge structures (Tau Ceti), the Weil representation, local theta modules and Kudla's splittings (MetaplecticAutomorphicForms), Arthur's classification (ML.4), the Jacquet–Langlands and base-change transfers for GL_2, and typed Hodge and Tate conjectures (MC.7). It has no cohomology of Shimura varieties with coefficients as an object of realizations, and no quaternionic Shimura varieties beyond curves. It also lacks exceptional isomorphisms, Kudla–Millson forms, quaternionic doubling and Siegel–Weil, Vogan–Zuckerman modules and Kottwitz's conjecture.

Routes: a new roadmap for the paper's main line; Part IIs of ShimuraVarieties (automorphic cohomology and its realizations) and of HilbertModularVarietiesAndShimuraCurves (quaternionic Shimura varieties for arbitrary Σ); a consumer route to the MetaplecticAutomorphicForms Part II proposed by Gan–Ichino; and sources for MP.3–MP.4, AF.4, ML.4, MC.2/MC.7 and GN.2. Eight mistakes are recorded. One is a gap in the proof of Theorem 12.4(ii): Galois does not act trivially on the components, but the argument is repaired using the Galois-invariance of c_η. One is a false bijection claim that is not used. The other six are misprints and definitional slips.
